message: "If you use this code, please cite it as below."
title: "Robust Neural Control via Flat Minima for Dynamical Systems (Pendubot)"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Joshi
    given-names: Omkar Anant
    affiliation: "Kingston University London"
license: GPL-3.0-only
repository-code: "https://github.com/OmkarJ48/Robust-Neural-Control-Via-Flat-Minima-For-Dynamical-Systems-Using-Pendubot-Model"
keywords:
  - robust control
  - neural network controller
  - flat minima
  - Pendubot
  - underactuated robotics
  - CasADi
  - MATLAB
abstract: >-
  MATLAB and CasADi code for an MSc dissertation (ME7743, MSc Mechatronic
  Systems, Kingston University London, 2025). A neural controller balances a
  Pendubot upright and is trained with a flatness criterion that penalises how
  sharply the closed-loop cost reacts to the plant parameters. Adam, a
  Yamashita-type projected flow and the null-space gradient flow of Feppon,
  Allaire and Dapogny are compared under the same simulator and cost.
